From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] adaptive: clamp the published PP verification budget to drafts

The last PP rank publishes `batch_draft_budget` as the authoritative
verification budget for the step, then decides whether the batch is partially
allocated with

    partial = pp_verification_budget not in (0, scheduled_drafts)

but it never reconciled that budget against `scheduled_drafts`, the number of
drafts the scheduler actually scheduled this step. Any step where the two differ
- a hot K=0 toggle, or a step whose drafts were dropped - has the manager
reporting a positive budget with `scheduled_drafts == 0`, so `partial` becomes
True and the step demands device-side `verification_lengths` for drafts that do
not exist, on every rank, with the schema check below it then failing or
verifying rows that were never proposed.

Clamp the published value to the drafts that exist. The scheduler is the single
source of truth for K; the adaptive manager sizes within it rather than
overriding it.

Found while integrating the tracing package, whose hot-K0 path needs this to be
correct on the last rank; the fix belongs to the adaptive series so the default
production build carries it too.

Signed-off-by: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
@@ -1659,6 +1659,12 @@
         if needs_pp_budget:
             pp_verification_budget = self.adaptive_verification.batch_draft_budget
             scheduled_drafts = sum(map(len, scheduler_output.scheduled_spec_decode_tokens.values()))
+            # The scheduler owns how many drafts exist this step: a hot K toggle or
+            # a step whose drafts were dropped can drive scheduled_drafts to zero
+            # while the manager still believes its budget is positive, which would
+            # read as a partial allocation with device lengths for drafts that do
+            # not exist. Clamp so a zero-draft step verifies zero rows.
+            pp_verification_budget = min(pp_verification_budget, scheduled_drafts)
             partial = pp_verification_budget not in (0, scheduled_drafts)
             if not self.is_first_pp_rank and partial != (pp_verification_lengths is not None):
                 raise RuntimeError("PP verification lengths/schema mismatch")
